22,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-036629","value":"13.45 ± 0.58","numeric":13.45}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"S1","value":0.208,"value_relation":"=","std":0.011,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1002/aoc.6759","year":2022,"record_id":"MLDB-002084","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipid-water partition coefficient was obtained by the standard shake flask method in the 1-octanol/ water system. In brief, the complexes were prepared with 1-octanol to obtain the solution of 20, 40, 60, 80, and 100 μM and drawing the standard curve according to the absorbance measured by UV/Vis. Next, the complex solutions (50 μM) prepared with an equal volume of 1-octanol/water saturated system were shaken at room temperature for 48 h. The mixed solutions were centrifuged at 2500 rpm/min for 15 min to separate the two phases. Determination of Cw used the absorbance of the lipid phase and a standard curve. The lipid phase concentration (Cw) could be obtained according to the absorbance of the lipid phase and the standard curve, and the water phase concentration (Co) could be determined by the principle of mass conservation. Obviously, the log P of the complexes was calculated by Equation (1)"}]}